e originally supposed to be part  of this whole city's make up since we do  have the info of the fact that Oslo is  getting its water supply from the lake  which is to the north of the city there  are two places where its garbage goes to  and there are some hydroelectric dams  just outside the city where much of the  electricity is coming from it's just  that none of these services can provide  it to the point that you would  realistically need them in-game for your  city not to crash down to rubble so  these are just certain things which are  kind of hard to overcome since you want  to hit that balance between on one hand  not getting a city that doesn't work in  game while on the other hand getting a  city that someone resembles Oslo also in  terms of services but yeah that's really  one of the quite difficult things which  I honestly can't really criticize city  skylines for in the end it's not really  a game where you're supposed to  perfectly recreate cities in and from a  gameplay perspective I think that the  balancing makes a lot of sense and if  you're just kind of creating a city over  time and just slowly growing bigger and  bigger with small neighborhoods I think  for a player of just a video game  other than a urban planner it makes much  more sense to take these things in a  very small scale but in my case where  I'm just creating a whole city in one go  it's creating a lot of issues not to  mention the whole traffic problem you  might notice later on that there is a  huge traffic jam that all go through  okay at some point in the future just  because everything is gonna move into  the city at the same time since  everything's kind of constructed at the  same time and they are all coming in  from the east from the connected  highways and moving into the city that  way say anthers there's lots of things  that the city kinda gets broken in game  just because I'm trying to make it like  in real life there's also one of the  issues is I'm using the Metro overhaul  to create a metro line that actually  goes above ground as well because even  though there are some underground metros  in Oslo most of the network is above  ground but the problem with that is that  you can't connect the metro lines to the  regular train lines which kind of does  happen at some parts so there's another  small thing which is very very very  difficult to get right in the game and  which I haven't really gotten a solution  for so far and then there's the issue of  water in hindsight I think I should have  just got on a mod which turns off the  water pipes altogether because it's very  obvious that you can't get realistic  water pipes in the game there's no way  to do that whatsoever and opting for  just trying to build everything with  perfect coverage is a lot more time  consuming than just getting a mod which  removes the need for water pipes  altogether but that's just a little bit  of an oversight on my part I thought it  would be a lot easier to just do this  kind of thing but kind of underestimated  just how big this city is because in the  end something to remember as well I  think is that even though Oslo is not an  enormous city in terms of well real  world scale the whole metropolitan area  I think is little over 2 million people  living in it in-game it's absolutely  huge and you definitely do need almost  the entire map to build this thing  so it's pretty large and truth be told I  definitely underestimated just how much  time it would take to build all of this  because of that by the way I should also  say right now this might very well be  the last episode of the series perhaps  I'll get a later episode out later but  the first stream is gonna be on the 16th  and before that I already wanna get a  final video out for this project but the  issue is that I'm currently recording  this commentary on my last day in the  Netherlands before I go to Los Angeles  for a week so I'll actually be in LA  when the streams are gonna happen and  because of that and also my university  things I kinda have to cram everything  into one weekend here and get as much  done as I can but to be honest for me  finishing oslo as far as possible is  more important than finishing this video  series so if I don't have any time to  finish more videos this might be the  last episode of this series even though  I will of course release a final video  and an overview of what the city looks  like in the end I hope though that this  will be the last interesting thing as  well since most of the rest of my  recordings is just suburbs and more  suburbs which all kind of more or less  looks the same so it's not like we're  missing out on the most important  elements but yeah in any case this might  be the last episode and after this will  suddenly jump to a completely finished  Oslo I'm sorry if that feels kind of  weird and it's a little it's a little  bit of a jarring way to end the series  but in my current situation I really  don't have much more time normally I  wouldn't really have a deadline so I can  always stretch out a series a little bit  more to neatly wrap up the videos but in  this case there's really a time before I  want to have everything out about this  so yeah if I'm right and this is the end  of it then I would love to thank you  guys for watching this really short  series of making Oslo I hope you enjoyed  it even though it's not quite the usual  fare and even if it's religious a short  series I'll end this with some final  cinematic  of a cone as it is right now and  hopefully I'll see you guys in the final  cinematic  [Music]  you
 

